Z||000000||phillip||07-02-2000||03:28 PM||||<BR>anybody got any emmisions stories pertaining to engine swaps. i guess this will only be for those who are in areas where emmisions test are done. it seem like a swap (especially a v8) would be easier without that worry. i think here once a car gets so old as long as it passes they don't look under the hood. it's posible my '84 could get away with it.||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||07-02-2000||08:13 PM||||1992 Buick Supercharged into a 1986 Olds Ciera GT.<P>What do you want to know?<P>In the process of swapping a 1993 3.4L DOHC into a 1986 Fiero SE.||||reg||1
Z||000002||phillip||07-02-2000||10:56 PM||||actualy, i asked about your 3.4 swap in another post. the one where someone wanted detailed swap info. as it pertains to this question i was just wondering if emmisions were a hassle on their own, especialy if you live some where that has vet testing. i guess i'm thinking with a larger engine would naturaly come more exhaust out put and may make the test harder to pass. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||07-03-2000||03:04 PM||||It will pass, just don't tell them it' a 3.4 when it should be a 2.8 and they won't know.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||07-04-2000||10:44 PM||||For passenger cars, I believe that the amount of emissions allowed depends on only the year model of the car, not the size of the engine. If the engine runs clean in the donor car, it should pass in your Fiero, as long as ALL of the emissions equipment is swapped in, as well. I believe there may be restrictions on swapping in an engine that is older than the car. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||07-05-2000||09:02 AM||||The official rules are that the emissions are tested by either the year of the car or the year of the engine, Which ever is newer. If the engine is older than the car it has to pass emissions for the year of the vehicle. Since all fiero's are 84-88 the emission levels are not bad to meet. For engines that are newer, say a 2000 3800SC,<BR>If you tell them it's a brand new engine they are suppose to test it as such. But they usually test it at the year of the vehicle.||||reg||1
